Helm Chart Repository – Complete Setup and Deployment Guide
Purpose: Create Helm charts, package them, publish them to GitHub using GitHub Pages, and install them on a Kubernetes cluster.

Example project: Payment and Shipping microservices

GitHub repository: https://github.com/Sachin-dev-hub/helm-repo

Helm repository URL: https://sachin-dev-hub.github.io/helm-repo/

1. Architecture and Workflow
The complete workflow:

Create Helm charts on your local machine.
Package charts into .tgz files.
Create a GitHub repository.
Upload chart packages and index.yaml.
Enable GitHub Pages.
Add the GitHub Pages URL to Helm on the Kubernetes machine.
Search and download charts.
Install applications on Kubernetes.
Verify deployments and pods.
2. Create Helm Chart Project
Create the project directory:


bash
mkdir helm-project
cd helm-project
Create two Helm charts:


bash
mkdir -p payment/templates
mkdir -p shipping/templates
Expected directory structure:


text
helm-project/
│
├── payment/
│   ├── Chart.yaml
│   ├── values.yaml
│   └── templates/
│       └── deployment.yaml
│
└── shipping/
    ├── Chart.yaml
    ├── values.yaml
    └── templates/
        └── deployment.yaml
3. Create Payment Helm Chart
File: payment/Chart.yaml

yaml
apiVersion: v2
name: payment
description: Helm chart for Payment Service
type: application
version: 0.1.0
appVersion: "1.0.0"
File: payment/values.yaml

yaml
image:
  repository: busybox
  tag: latest
  pullPolicy: IfNotPresent

appMessage: "Payments Service"
File: payment/templates/deployment.yaml

yaml
apiVersion: apps/v1
kind: Deployment
metadata:
  name: {{ .Release.Name }}-{{ .Chart.Name }}
  labels:
    app: {{ .Chart.Name }}
spec:
  replicas: 1
  selector:
    matchLabels:
      app: {{ .Chart.Name }}
  template:
    metadata:
      labels:
        app: {{ .Chart.Name }}
    spec:
      containers:
        - name: {{ .Chart.Name }}
          image: "{{ .Values.image.repository }}:{{ .Values.image.tag }}"
          command: ['sh', '-c', 'echo {{ .Values.appMessage }}; sleep 3600']
          imagePullPolicy: {{ .Values.image.pullPolicy }}
4. Create Shipping Helm Chart
File: shipping/Chart.yaml

yaml
apiVersion: v2
name: shipping
description: Helm chart for Shipping Service
type: application
version: 0.1.0
appVersion: "1.0.0"
File: shipping/values.yaml

yaml
image:
  repository: busybox
  tag: latest
  pullPolicy: IfNotPresent

appMessage: "Shipping Service"
File: shipping/templates/deployment.yaml

yaml
apiVersion: apps/v1
kind: Deployment
metadata:
  name: {{ .Release.Name }}-{{ .Chart.Name }}
  labels:
    app: {{ .Chart.Name }}
spec:
  replicas: 1
  selector:
    matchLabels:
      app: {{ .Chart.Name }}
  template:
    metadata:
      labels:
        app: {{ .Chart.Name }}
    spec:
      containers:
        - name: {{ .Chart.Name }}
          image: "{{ .Values.image.repository }}:{{ .Values.image.tag }}"
          command: ['sh', '-c', 'echo {{ .Values.appMessage }}; sleep 3600']
          imagePullPolicy: {{ .Values.image.pullPolicy }}
5. Validate Helm Charts
Run these commands from helm-project:


bash
helm lint payment
helm lint shipping
Expected:


text
1 chart(s) linted, 0 chart(s) failed
Test template rendering:


bash
helm template payment-release ./payment
helm template shipping-release ./shipping
These commands generate Kubernetes YAML without installing anything.

6. Package Helm Charts
Package both charts:


bash
helm package payment
helm package shipping
Generated files:


text
payment-0.1.0.tgz
shipping-0.1.0.tgz
The .tgz files are the packaged Helm charts that will be published.

7. Create GitHub Helm Repository
Create a GitHub repository:


text
helm-repo
Example:

https://github.com/Sachin-dev-hub/helm-repo

Clone it on your machine:


bash
cd /root

git clone https://github.com/Sachin-dev-hub/helm-repo.git
Enter the repository:


bash
cd helm-repo
Copy the packaged charts:


bash
cp /root/helm-project/payment-0.1.0.tgz .
cp /root/helm-project/shipping-0.1.0.tgz .
Expected structure:


text
helm-repo/
│
├── payment-0.1.0.tgz
├── shipping-0.1.0.tgz
└── README.md
8. Generate Helm Repository index.yaml
This is an important step.

Helm requires an index.yaml file to identify available charts and their download locations.

Run:


bash
helm repo index . \
  --url https://sachin-dev-hub.github.io/helm-repo/
This generates:


text
helm-repo/
├── index.yaml
├── payment-0.1.0.tgz
├── shipping-0.1.0.tgz
└── README.md
Check the generated index:


bash
cat index.yaml
It should contain entries for:

payment
shipping
The chart download URLs should point to GitHub Pages, for example:


text
https://sachin-dev-hub.github.io/helm-repo/payment-0.1.0.tgz
9. Configure Git and Push to GitHub
Configure Git identity (first time only):


bash
git config --global user.name "Sachin Maskar"
git config --global user.email "YOUR_GITHUB_EMAIL"
Check the remote:


bash
git remote -v
Expected:


text
origin https://github.com/Sachin-dev-hub/helm-repo.git
Stage files:


bash
git add .
Commit:


bash
git commit -m "Add payment and shipping Helm charts"
Push:


bash
git push origin main
Authentication note: GitHub HTTPS authentication requires a Personal Access Token or another supported authentication method, not your normal GitHub account password.

10. Enable GitHub Pages
Open:

https://github.com/Sachin-dev-hub/helm-repo

Follow these steps:

Open Settings.
Select Pages.
Under Build and deployment, choose Deploy from a branch.
Select branch main.
Select folder / (root).
Click Save.
GitHub Pages will publish your Helm repository.

Your repository URL becomes:


text
https://sachin-dev-hub.github.io/helm-repo/
Verify the index:


bash
curl -I https://sachin-dev-hub.github.io/helm-repo/index.yaml
Expected HTTP status:


text
200 OK
11. Add Helm Repository on Kubernetes Machine
Switch to your Kubernetes lab machine.

Add the Helm repository:


bash
helm repo add myrepo \
https://sachin-dev-hub.github.io/helm-repo/
Expected:


text
"myrepo" has been added to your repositories
Update repository:


bash
helm repo update
List repositories:


bash
helm repo list
Expected:


text
NAME     URL
myrepo   https://sachin-dev-hub.github.io/helm-repo/
12. Search Available Helm Charts
Run:


bash
helm search repo myrepo
Expected:


text
NAME             CHART VERSION   APP VERSION
myrepo/payment   0.1.0           1.0.0
myrepo/shipping  0.1.0           1.0.0
You can also search all versions:


bash
helm search repo myrepo --versions
13. Install Helm Charts on Kubernetes
Install Payment:


bash
helm install payment-release myrepo/payment
Install Shipping:


bash
helm install shipping-release myrepo/shipping
Check installation:


bash
helm list -A
Expected releases:


text
payment-release
shipping-release
14. Verify Kubernetes Deployments
Check deployments:


bash
kubectl get deployments
Expected:


text
NAME                        READY   UP-TO-DATE   AVAILABLE
payment-release-payment     1/1     1            1
shipping-release-shipping   1/1     1            1
Check pods:


bash
kubectl get pods
Check application logs:


bash
kubectl logs deployment/payment-release-payment
Expected:


text
Payments Service
Shipping:


bash
kubectl logs deployment/shipping-release-shipping
Expected:


text
Shipping Service
Note: These example BusyBox containers print their messages and sleep for 3600 seconds. They are not HTTP servers.

15. Important Helm Commands

Purpose	Command
List Helm repositories	helm repo list
Update repositories	helm repo update
Search charts	helm search repo myrepo
List releases	helm list -A
Check release	helm status payment-release
View chart values	helm get values payment-release
View deployed manifest	helm get manifest payment-release
Upgrade release	helm upgrade payment-release myrepo/payment
Rollback release	helm rollback payment-release 1
Uninstall release	helm uninstall payment-release
Validate chart	helm lint payment
Render templates	helm template payment-release ./payment
Package chart	helm package payment
16. How to Publish a New Chart Version
Whenever you modify a chart, follow this process.

Step 1: Update Chart.yaml
For example:


yaml
version: 0.1.1
Increase the chart version whenever you publish a new chart package.

Step 2: Validate

bash
helm lint payment
helm lint shipping
Step 3: Package

bash
helm package payment
helm package shipping
Step 4: Copy new packages into GitHub repository

bash
cp payment-0.1.1.tgz /root/helm-repo/
cp shipping-0.1.1.tgz /root/helm-repo/
Run these commands from the appropriate directory or use absolute paths.

Step 5: Regenerate index.yaml
Inside helm-repo:


bash
helm repo index . \
  --url https://sachin-dev-hub.github.io/helm-repo/
Step 6: Push updated repository

bash
git add .
git commit -m "Release Helm charts version 0.1.1"
git push origin main
Step 7: Update Kubernetes Helm repository

bash
helm repo update
helm search repo myrepo --versions
Step 8: Upgrade installed applications

bash
helm upgrade payment-release myrepo/payment
helm upgrade shipping-release myrepo/shipping
If necessary, specify a particular version:


bash
helm upgrade payment-release myrepo/payment --version 0.1.1
17. Troubleshooting
Problem 1: Helm repository returns 404
Incorrect:


bash
helm repo add myrepo https://github.com/Sachin-dev-hub/helm-repo.git
Correct:


bash
helm repo add myrepo https://sachin-dev-hub.github.io/helm-repo/
Check:


bash
curl -I https://sachin-dev-hub.github.io/helm-repo/index.yaml
Problem 2: No repositories found
Error:


text
Error: no repositories found.
Solution:


bash
helm repo add myrepo https://sachin-dev-hub.github.io/helm-repo/
helm repo update
Problem 3: Chart is not showing in search
Check:


bash
cat index.yaml
helm repo update
helm search repo myrepo
Make sure the chart package exists and index.yaml includes the chart.

Problem 4: Chart changes are not appearing
Remember:

Increase version in Chart.yaml.
Package the chart again.
Copy the new package to GitHub repository.
Regenerate index.yaml.
Commit and push.
Wait for GitHub Pages to publish.
Run helm repo update.
Problem 5: Git says Author identity unknown
Configure:


bash
git config --global user.name "Sachin Maskar"
git config --global user.email "YOUR_GITHUB_EMAIL"
Then commit again.

18. Complete Command Reference – Quick Execution
This is the short workflow to follow whenever you create or publish Helm charts.

LOCAL MACHINE – Create and package


bash
helm lint payment
helm lint shipping

helm package payment
helm package shipping
GITHUB REPOSITORY – Publish


bash
cd /root/helm-repo

cp /root/helm-project/payment-0.1.0.tgz .
cp /root/helm-project/shipping-0.1.0.tgz .

helm repo index . \
  --url https://sachin-dev-hub.github.io/helm-repo/

git add .
git commit -m "Publish Helm charts"
git push origin main
KUBERNETES MACHINE – Pull and install


bash
helm repo add myrepo \
https://sachin-dev-hub.github.io/helm-repo/

helm repo update

helm search repo myrepo

helm install payment-release myrepo/payment

helm install shipping-release myrepo/shipping
VERIFY


bash
helm list -A

kubectl get deployments

kubectl get pods

kubectl get svc
